# TLS certificates. tests/fixtures/regenerate.sh makes them. The repository
# never holds them. If a repository holds the private key of a certificate
# authority, then anyone with a copy of that repository can sign with that key.
# A machine that trusted such an authority, for example a browser, would then
# accept a certificate for any site.
tests/fixtures/*.pem
tests/fixtures/*.csr
tests/fixtures/*.srl
# The incorrect files also stay out of the repository. Two of them are copies
# of the real certificate and the real key.
tests/fixtures/bad/
tests/fixtures/trust/
# The coverage jobs collect the gcov data of each configuration here.
# tests/coverage-all.sh uses a temporary directory and leaves nothing behind.
coverage-data/
